OriginLore (
    origin_id: "silica_xenofauna",
    canonical_name: "Silica Xenofauna",
    physical_description: "A loose grouping of non-Crystalfold silicate-based sentient organisms identified by the Collegium across the inner Sol system, primarily in Vulcan magma vents and the deep heat zones of Mercury's orbital boundary. Body presents in a wide range of forms, but typical adult specimens are between 1.5 and 4.0 meters in length, with silicate exoskeletons, internal magma-circulation systems, and the ability to consume dissolved heavy metals as a primary energy source. Eyes are crystalline and respond to infrared rather than visible-light wavelengths. Lifespan is approximately five hundred Earth-years for documented adults; reproduction occurs through silicate seed-shedding in active magma vents.",
    cultural_traits: "The silica xenofauna are, by the Collegium's classification, a distant kin to the Crystalfold — both originate from silicon-based biochemistry, but the xenofauna predate the Crystalfold awakening by an estimated ten thousand Earth-years, and their cognitive architecture is, by every available reading, fundamentally different. The xenofauna do not maintain a resonance link comparable to the Crystalfold; they communicate, when they communicate at all, through patterns of infrared display and direct silicate-tissue contact. The xenofauna have, in fifty years of Concordat contact, declined to engage in any formal diplomatic exchange. They tolerate Concordat researchers in their vents under conditions the xenofauna do not fully explain; they refuse, by their own internal protocols, to allow sample extraction without consent that has, in fifty years, been granted exactly three times. The Crystalfold consider the silica xenofauna distant kin and have, on multiple occasions, refused to allow Collegium sampling of the xenofauna without xenofauna consent. The Collegium considers the silica xenofauna the most intellectually intriguing sentient organism in the Sol system and has, in writing, requested permission to establish a long-term research relationship.",
    gameplay_strengths: "Substantial heat tolerance (operates comfortably at temperatures up to 1200 Kelvin). Strong radiation resistance. Resistance to most chemical hazards. Strong cold-environment dormancy (can survive sustained cold periods in inert state). Native infrared vision. Strong physical durability (silicate exoskeleton).",
    gameplay_weaknesses: "Vulnerable to cold-environment operations (slowed metabolism). Cannot operate effectively in oxygen-rich, low-heat environments. Limited compatibility with all other origin medical interventions. No native communication with Concordat factions (silicate-language barrier). Restricted gear compatibility (cannot wear most human equipment). Reproduction requires specific magma-vent access.",
    home_world: "Vulcan magma vents (canonical primary); secondary populations identified at Mercury orbital boundary and reportedly in the deeper Europa hydrothermal vent network.",
    notable_origins_in_corefall_universe: [
        "Designated Specimen V-Forge-1 (the only silica xenofauna currently in Collegium archive; preserved under Crystalfold consent)",
        "The xenofauna communities of the Vulcan deep heat caverns (no individual names recorded in Concordat documents)",
        "Reportedly observed in the Europa Tara-cavern hydrothermal zone (unconfirmed; Bouchard has, in private, indicated additional observations)",
    ],
)
